      "y": 4.6,
      "w": 2.2,
      "z": 3,
      "md": "estimated new revenue each year. About 90% would come from the top 1% of households.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11.5,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bul3",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 5.6000000000000005,
      "y": 5.73,
      "w": 2.2,
      "z": 3,
      "md": "Gains from selling stocks and land are **capped at 7.25%**; wages are taxed up to **13%**.\n\nAct 24 (2026) left gains alone, so the gap grew from 3.75 to **5.75 points**.\n\n**Most local families would pay nothing more.**",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 12,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suph3",
      "page": 1,
